    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.select_last_nodes_created - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.select_last_nodes_created.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.select_last_nodes_created()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Select the last N nodes that were created.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.select_last_nodes_created()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Select the last N nodes that were created.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.select_last_nodes_created()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Select the last N nodes that were created.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nSelect the last N nodes that were created.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L30279-L30393){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.select_last_nodes_created(\n    n,\n    set_op=\"union\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Select last nodes created](../assets/graphs/select-last-nodes-created.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Six nodes A to F with filled badges 1 to 6 giving the order in which they were created. select_last_nodes_created(2) selects the two most recent, E and F, drawn in the accent color.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nSelects the `n` most recently created nodes. The graph keeps\ntrack of the order in which nodes were added (see `get_node_creation_order()`), and this\nmethod takes the tail of that order. Nodes that have since been deleted are skipped, so\nthe selection always refers to nodes that still exist.\n\nThis is handy in incremental, build-as-you-go workflows, for example to:\n\n- tag or style the nodes that a generator such as `add_path_graph()` or\n  `add_star_graph()` just added, with `set_node_attrs_ws()`\n- connect a freshly added batch of nodes to each other with `fully_connect_nodes_ws()`\n- undo the last few additions with `delete_nodes_ws()`\n\nSelection is based on creation order, not on node IDs or labels. The nodes are added to\nthe current selection, unless `set_op=` says otherwise. The graph is modified in place\nand returned for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[n]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of most recently created nodes to select. Must be a non-negative integer (a\n    negative value raises `ValueError`). If `n` is larger than the number of nodes,\n    every node is selected; `n=0` selects nothing.\n\n<code>[set_op]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;union&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   How these nodes combine with the current node selection. `\"union\"` (default) adds them\n    to it, `\"replace\"` makes them the selection, `\"intersect\"` keeps only the selected nodes\n    among them, and `\"difference\"` removes them from it. Any edge selection is cleared,\n    since the graph holds a selection of nodes or of edges but not both.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The same graph (modified in place) for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `set_op=` is not `\"union\"`, `\"replace\"`, `\"intersect\"`, or `\"difference\"`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~select_last_edges_created`) \n\n:   Select the edges made last.\n\n[](`~set_node_attrs_ws`) \n\n:   Set attributes on the selected nodes.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThis selects the two nodes added last, here `A` and `B`. It goes by when the nodes were\nmade, not by their labels:\n\n::: {#8408c105 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_nodes([\"D\", \"C\", \"A\", \"B\"])\ngraph.select_last_nodes_created(2)\n\nsorted(graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in graph.get_selected_node_ids())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['A', 'B']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nA common use is to tag what a generator just added. Only the three nodes of the new path\nget `batch=2`:\n\n::: {#d9744924 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph = (\n    ec.Graph()\n    .add_node(label=\"root\", batch=1)\n    .add_path_graph(3)\n    .select_last_nodes_created(3)\n    .set_node_attrs_ws(batch=2)\n)\n\ngraph.get_node_df().select(\"label\", \"batch\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>batch</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;root&quot;</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;2&quot;</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;3&quot;</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;4&quot;</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A new branch line\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, each station placed at its `pos` on the map.\nThe city plans to run the Red line two stops further west, past Westgate. Selecting the\nlast two stations made picks out the new ones, to mark them as planned:\n\n::: {#a7fd898b .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\n(\n    metro\n    .add_node(label=\"Brookfield\", pos=[-8.0, 0.0], lines=[\"Red\"])\n    .add_node(label=\"Quarry\", pos=[-10.0, 0.0], lines=[\"Red\"])\n    .add_edges(\n        [(\"Westgate\", \"Brookfield\", 4), (\"Brookfield\", \"Quarry\", 3)]\n    )\n    .select_last_nodes_created(2)\n    .set_node_attrs_ws(planned=True)\n)\n\nmetro.get_node_df().select(\"label\", \"planned\").tail(3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (3, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>planned</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>bool</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Airport&quot;</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Brookfield&quot;</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Quarry&quot;</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#dbcb63ff .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", highlight=\"planned\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,4